  "result": "Perfect! I found the source file that decides the per-person list of menu entries. \n\nThe file `src/config/nav.ts` contains the `visibleNav()` function, which is the central place that filters navigation items based on:\n\n1. **Permissions** - using the `can()` function to check if an actor (user) can perform an action based on their role (admin vs viewer)\n2. **Feature flags** - using the `flagAllows()` function to check if a feature is enabled for the user's organization plan\n\nThe sidebar component (`src/components/domain/nav/app-sidebar.tsx`) calls `visibleNav()` to filter both `SIDEBAR_NAV` and `SETTINGS_NAV` arrays. As noted in the file's comment: \"`visibleNav()` is the only place that decides what a given actor sees.\"\n\nEach navigation item declares:\n- An `action` (permission required)\n- A `flag` (feature flag that gates it)\n\nThe `visibleNav()` function recursively filters items based on these criteria, ensuring that users only see menu entries they have permission to access and that are available for their plan.\n\nANSWER: src/config/nav.ts",
